:: RAM-model x w_3 x policy study.
::
:: Runs placement + selection simulation for runs 300..323, i.e. for every cell
:: generated by ram_w3_experiments.py:
::     RAM capacity model : off (aggregate) / l2 (eligibility + l2 norm)
::     w_3                : 0.5 1.0 1.5 2.0 2.5 3.0
::     selection policy   : deterministic / stochastic
::
:: Afterwards every placement is re-simulated on 10 independent request streams
:: (resimulate_seeds.py, no re-solving) so the figure can show confidence
:: intervals rather than single noisy runs.
::
:: Generate the parameter files first:  ram_w3_experiments.py
:: Visualize the results afterwards:    visualization_ram_w3.py
::
:: PY points at the checkout's virtual environment; adapt it to your own setup
:: (the older batch files in this repo hard-code an absolute anaconda path).
@echo off
setlocal
set PY=.optifaasvenv\Scripts\python.exe

for /l %%x in (300, 1, 323) do (
    echo === run %%x ===
    %PY% placement.py --num_run=%%x
    %PY% selection_simulation.py --num_run=%%x
)

%PY% resimulate_seeds.py --seeds=10

echo.
echo Study complete. Draw the figure with:
echo     %PY% visualization_ram_w3.py
endlocal
